=====================================================================
2. HOW THE MAIN FEATURES WORK
=====================================================================

Pattern everywhere: Route -> Controller (validate + respond) -> Service (logic) -> Model.
Services return ['status' => bool, 'message' => ..., ...].

Cart (CartService):
- Owner = user_id if logged in, else session_id (guests can shop).
- Same product + variant again -> qty increases (firstOrNew), capped at stock.
- Product with variants must have one selected.
- Coupon code + shipping method are kept in the session.
- Coupon is re-checked every time totals are calculated.
- Shipping rates: free 0 / standard 10 / express 20 (CartService::SHIPPING_RATES).

Wishlist (WishlistService):
- Same owner rule as cart. One click = toggle (add or remove).
- Variant optional.

Guest -> login merge:
- On OTP login (OtpController::verify) the guest cart + wishlist move to the user.
- Guest orders are linked to the account by email (safe because OTP proved the email).

Accounts - one per email and one per phone number:
- Email: unique index + validation everywhere (register, my account, admin
  profile, checkout "create account"). MySQL compares case-insensitively.
- Phone: User::normalizePhone() strips spaces/dashes/brackets before saving
  (model mutator) and before validating, so "98765 43210" = "9876543210".
  Unique index + validation in the same places. Format: 7-15 digits, optional "+".
  Limit: "+919876543210" and "9876543210" still count as different numbers.
- Google login reuses the account with the same email instead of creating a new one.

Placing an order (OrderService::createOrder):
- DB::transaction + lockForUpdate() on stock rows -> no overselling when two
  people buy the last item at the same time. Any failure = full rollback.
- Creates order + items, reduces stock, increases coupon used_count, clears cart.
- Confirmation email is sent AFTER the transaction (mail failure never undoes an order).

Online payments (PaymentService::completePayment):
- Browser redirect AND webhook both confirm the payment.
- Cache lock + "order already exists?" check -> exactly one order is created.
- Webhooks are trusted by signature, so they are CSRF-exempt (bootstrap/app.php).

Order status (Order::NEXT_STATUSES):
  pending -> processing -> shipped -> delivered
  pending / processing -> cancelled
- delivered + COD -> payment marked paid automatically.
- cancelled -> stock + coupon use given back once (stock_restored flag).

Exports (ExportService):
- CSV is streamed + chunk(500) -> big exports use little memory.
  UTF-8 BOM at the start so Excel shows the rupee sign correctly.
- PDF via dompdf, max 1000 rows (PDF_ROW_LIMIT) - use CSV for more.

Home page content (HomeSettingService):
- schema() drives the admin form: add a field there + a migration column and it
  appears in Admin > Home Settings automatically (tabs, labels, validation).
- home_setting('key'), home_asset('key') (upload or placeholder), home_link('link').
- home_link(): empty or "#" -> fallback link (Shop Now buttons fall back to /products).

Maintenance mode (Admin > System Settings, or artisan down / up):
- Admin\MaintenanceController runs artisan down/up in-process (works without proc_open).
- Paths that stay open: Http\Middleware\PreventRequestsDuringMaintenance
  ($except = admin, admin/*, webhooks/*, payment/*). Kept in that class on purpose:
  "artisan down" copies the list into storage/framework/down, so the pre-rendered
  page (served before Laravel boots) lets them through from admin, terminal or CI.
- Each enable creates a new 32-char secret -> private preview link shown in admin.
- Yellow reminder bar on every admin page while the store is offline.

Error pages + database outages:
- resources/views/errors/*.blade.php (404, 403, 419, 429, 500, 503) use their own
  layout (errors/layout) - no database, no Vite, no site header - so they still work
  when those are broken. Dark-mode logo via <picture>.
- 503 has two texts: maintenance (default) and $reason = 'database'. Both reload every 30s.
- Support\DatabaseUnavailable + the render() handler in bootstrap/app.php: a refused /
  lost / timed-out DB connection -> 503 "temporarily unavailable" (JSON for AJAX)
  instead of 500. A bad SQL query is still a 500 (that's a bug, not an outage).
  Only when APP_DEBUG=false - locally you still get the debug page.
- config/database.php: PDO::ATTR_TIMEOUT = DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT (default 5s).

Admin form buttons (public/admin_assets/js/form-loading.js):
- Normal (page-reload) forms: clicked button shows spinner + "Processing...",
  other submit buttons disabled. AJAX forms, GET filters and cancelled confirms
  are left alone. Opt out with <form data-no-loading> (needed for POST downloads).

