3. ENVIRONMENT NOTES
=====================================================================

- Only ONE env template: .env.example. Local values; every line that must
  change on a server has a "# PRODUCTION:" comment above it.
- AppServiceProvider::configureEnvironment() = the place for local vs live behaviour:
    production -> https:// links forced, migrate:fresh / db:wipe blocked.
  Staging is NOT production -> set APP_FORCE_HTTPS=true (and SESSION_SECURE_COOKIE=true)
  in staging's .env yourself.
- APP_DEBUG is NOT automatic. Must be false on every server.
- Mail must be real SMTP on the server - login OTP is sent by email.
- After any .env change on a server: php artisan optimize
  (when config is cached, env() returns null outside config files).
- Telescope (dev package) only loads when APP_ENV=local.
- Seeders: never plain "db:seed" on a live database (demo data). AdminUserSeeder needs
  ADMIN_SEED_PASSWORD (12+ chars) in .env - put it there only while seeding.
- QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync (no worker on shared hosting), no scheduled tasks, no cron.

Payment URLs:
- In config/services.php (not hardcoded in gateway classes).
- Still TEST/SANDBOX mode. To go live: live keys + PAYPAL_SANDBOX=false
  + INSTAMOJO_SANDBOX=false. No code change.
- Webhooks: /webhooks/{razorpay|stripe|paypal|instamojo}, one per site.
  In test mode the gateways send events to ALL webhooks -> each site ignores
  payments it doesn't know (just a log line).

Bugsnag (error monitoring):
- Server .env: LOG_STACK=daily,bugsnag + BUGSNAG_API_KEY
- Reports only from production/staging, only error level and above.
- Locally it never sends (stage = local).

LogDNAService: not used anywhere. Safe to delete later.

