- Each site is a separate Hostinger "website" (own PHP settings, SSL, folder).
  Staging was NOT made with Domains > Subdomains: that form only allows folders
  inside public_html, which is a link into production's public/ folder.
- PHP 8.4, memory_limit 512M, uploads 20M - set per website in hPanel.
- Staging data is a COPY of production taken on 04 Oct 2026. It drifts over time.
  Refresh staging from production (replaces all staging data):
    mysqldump -u <prod_db_user> -p --single-transaction --no-tablespaces u279378759_selfbuy > ~/staging-copy.sql
    mysql -u <staging_db_user> -p u279378759_staging < ~/staging-copy.sql
    rm ~/staging-copy.sql
  Data never moves between the sites by itself - only code does (through git).

Hostinger limits (shared hosting) and the workarounds:
- proc_open disabled -> composer install --no-scripts, then php artisan package:discover
                        (php artisan about also fails; use config:show / env instead)
- symlink() disabled -> ln -s ../storage/app/public public/storage (not storage:link)
- No sudo, SSH only inside the home folder.
- MySQL 8 dumps from the Mac: add --set-gtid-purged=OFF --no-tablespaces and skip the
  telescope_* tables, otherwise phpMyAdmin stops with "BINLOG ADMIN privilege".

GitHub (repo is PRIVATE):
- Server -> GitHub: read-only deploy key ~/.ssh/github_deploy on the server
  ("hostinger-server" in repo Settings > Deploy keys). Both sites use it.
- GitHub Actions -> server: key "github-actions" (added in hPanel > SSH Keys).
- Repo secrets: SSH_HOST, SSH_PORT, SSH_USER, SSH_PRIVATE_KEY, SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS.
- Environments: production (branch master), staging (branch develop),
  each with variable DEPLOY_PATH.
- Free plan + private repo = no "required reviewers" and no branch protection.
  The manual "Run workflow" click is the production approval.

What a deploy does (.github/workflows/deploy.yml):
  build CSS/JS + tests on a fresh MySQL -> SSH -> maintenance on (kept on if an admin
  had switched it on) -> git reset --hard to the tested commit -> composer install
  --no-dev --no-scripts + package:discover -> rsync public/build -> migrate --force
  -> optimize -> maintenance off.
- Deploy history on each server: storage/logs/deploy.log (START / SUCCESS / FAILED).
- Failed deploy: site stays on the maintenance page, "Diagnostics" step shows the
  last Laravel log lines. Fix + push, or "Re-run jobs". Emergency: php artisan up.
- git reset --hard discards edits made directly on the server to tracked files.
  Never edit code on the server - only .env, through SSH / File Manager.

Third-party settings per site:
- Google OAuth client: redirect URIs for selfbuy.live, staging.selfbuy.live and
  http://127.0.0.1:8000 (local). Each .env: GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI="${APP_URL}/auth/google/callback".
  Locally open the site at http://127.0.0.1:8000 (Google rejects .test domains).
- Webhooks registered in Stripe / Razorpay / PayPal for both sites, separate secrets.
- Email: no-reply@selfbuy.live (Hostinger mail), smtp.hostinger.com:465 ssl.

=====================================================================
5. DAILY WORKFLOW
=====================================================================

1. git checkout develop, work + test locally, commit, push
2. CI deploys staging -> test on staging.selfbuy.live
3. GitHub: Pull request develop -> master ("Release: ..."), tests must be green,
   review "Files changed", Merge (merge commit, keep the develop branch)
4. Actions > CI/CD > Run workflow (master) -> production
5. Locally: git checkout master && git pull; git checkout develop && git pull

New migration? Test it on staging first - it runs on production only after step 4.
New .env key? Add it to .env.example AND to both servers' .env before deploying.

